Description: Try Linux V4L2 H.264 encoders before software for MP4 and MOV
 V4L2 mem2mem encoders do not expose an AVHWDeviceType and their available
 formats depend on the device the FFmpeg wrapper opens. Try common 8-bit
 4:2:0 layouts when setting up a recorder, without advertising formats or
 requiring a named device. Request an appropriate bitrate and H.264 level.
 Keep the usual fallback when no V4L2 encoder can open.
Forwarded: no

